Plinius: device facts, scale steps and notch for the phone.

- About: processor name from the device package (ARM's /proc/cpuinfo has no model name),
  installed RAM from the device tree instead of MemTotal, no "vm-other" virtualization row,
  disk capacity from the largest LUN of a UFS drive (udisks reports the 4 MB boot LUN).
- Display: the built-in panel offers 100-200 % of a base scale from the device package
  (Plinius: 200 % = scale 3) instead of 100-300 % in nine steps; new "Notch" row for
  phosh-plinius (org.plinius.display).
- No "Multitasking" panel: workspaces and hot corners are GNOME Shell features.

The helpers (cc-plinius-device.*) live as separate files in the package directory and are
copied to panels/common/ in prepare().

